    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, but the clear anchor for our lineup is **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency score makes him our premier play. Facing a favorable matchup against Fedde (5.20 xERA), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from both a high-ceiling park factor and a substantial SP skill edge, making him the cornerstone of our pursuit of Roto category gains. **Kyle Tucker** (76.93) and **Andy Pages** (72.17) also profile as high-end starters; both benefit from a generous park environment against Springs, and **Andy Pages**\u2019 spot at the #2 hole provides the necessary plate appearance volume to capitalize on his current efficiency projection. **Miguel Vargas** (66.77) also grades out strongly, with his 0.370 xwOBA suggesting he is primed to exploit the matchup against Gibson.\n\nStrategic prioritization of speed remains a focal point of our daily selection. While **Nasim Nunez** (45.92) carries a lower raw score, his deployment is essential due to the 88% stolen base success probability against a slow-delivering pitcher, justifying his inclusion despite the #8 lineup anchor. Conversely, the bench decision regarding **Curtis Mead** (39.15) was the tightest call of the day. **Curtis Mead** fell just shy of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor for starting consideration; while his park factor is beneficial, the negative platoon impact and SP skill differential against Early effectively neutralized his utility, cementing his role as a depth piece for this specific matchup.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the risks inherent in today's volatility. **Nolan Schanuel** (42.30) and **Jackson Merrill** (44.97) are operating near the bottom of our starting threshold, hampered by tough matchups against Woo and Boyd, respectively. Furthermore, we are continuing to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and we have confirmed **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** will remain on the bench as he is not currently slated for a start. Managers should keep a close eye on the weather and official lineup confirmations for **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks**, as any unexpected shifts in the batting order could necessitate a pivot to our bench depth to ensure we remain within our daily game cap constraints.",
